Realtime subscription callbacks in `userNearbyRestaurant.ts` were calling `fetchRestaurants()` without error handling, causing failures to be silently swallowed.

## Changes

- Added `.catch()` handlers to all `fetchRestaurants()` calls in Supabase realtime event listeners
- Each handler logs descriptive error messages identifying the triggering event (INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on ravintolat/menus tables)

```typescript
// Before
.on("postgres_changes", { event: "INSERT", schema: "public", table: "ravintolat" }, (payload) => {
  console.log("ravintolat INSERT:", payload);
  fetchRestaurants();
})

// After
.on("postgres_changes", { event: "INSERT", schema: "public", table: "ravintolat" }, (payload) => {
  console.log("ravintolat INSERT:", payload);
  fetchRestaurants().catch((err) => {
    console.error("Error fetching restaurants after INSERT:", err);
  });
})
```

Applied to all 5 event handlers: ravintolat INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE and menus INSERT/UPDATE.

