When `geolocation.watchPosition` encounters an error or returns invalid coordinates, the `userLocation` state was not cleared, causing stale location data to persist.

## Changes

- Set `userLocation` to `null` when coordinates fail `isValidLat`/`isValidLng` validation
- Set `userLocation` to `null` in the geolocation error callback

```typescript
navigator.geolocation.watchPosition(
  (pos) => {
    const lat = pos.coords.latitude;
    const lng = pos.coords.longitude;
    if (isValidLat(lat) && isValidLng(lng)) {
      setUserLocation({ lat, lng });
    } else {
      setUserLocation(null);  // Clear stale data
    }
  },
  (err) => {
    console.warn("Sijaintia ei saatu:", err);
    setUserLocation(null);  // Clear on error
  },
  { enableHighAccuracy: true, maximumAge: 10_000, timeout: 10_000 }
);
```

